<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns">
  <data key="gFormat">Cyberiada-GraphML-1.0</data>
  <key id="gFormat" for="graphml" attr.name="format" attr.type="string"/>
  <key id="dName" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string"/>
  <key id="dName" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string"/>
  <key id="dStateMachine" for="graph" attr.name="stateMachine"/>
  <key id="dNote" for="node" attr.name="note" attr.type="string"/>
  <key id="dVertex" for="node" attr.name="vertex" attr.type="string"/>
  <key id="dData" for="node" attr.name="data" attr.type="string"/>
  <key id="dData" for="edge" attr.name="data" attr.type="string"/>
  <graph id="G" edgedefault="directed">
    <data key="dStateMachine"/>
    <data key="dName">Draw</data>
    <node id="d_meta">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_META</data>
      <data key="dData">standardVersion/ 1.0

platform/ CybersphereAgents

platformLanguage/ Python

name/ Draw</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_agent">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT agent</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Agent</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_loop">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT loop</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Loop</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_tools">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT tools</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Tools</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_prompt">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT prompt</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Prompt</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_log">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT log</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Log</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_document">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT document</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Document</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_oracle">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT oracle</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Oracle

profile/ stress</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_c_register">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT register</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Register</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_p_draw">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">PROMPT draw</data>
      <data key="dData">Draw the diagram described in the task as a clean hierarchical state machine
under the state machine G0: the states, the nesting, the pseudostates, the
transitions and the actions, following the shape given. Keep the layout tidy:
children inside their parents with a margin, siblings apart, no overlaps.

The editor keeps a diagram well-formed; draw so these hold, and the
editor will maintain them for you:
  - a child sits inside its parent with a margin; a parent grows to fit its
    children and never shrinks below them [NODE-1, NODE-2]
  - sibling elements do not overlap; keep them apart [NODE-6, NODE-7]
  - one initial pseudostate per state (or per the top machine) [SEM-1]; a
    transition's endpoints are legal kinds - nothing leaves a final, nothing
    enters an initial [SEM-2]; a choice's outgoing transitions are guarded with
    one [else] branch [SEM-3]
  - a state's name is non-empty and unique among its siblings [STRUCT-2]; every
    element has one parent, no cycles [STRUCT-3]; a composite state has children,
    a leaf is simple or a pseudostate [STRUCT-6]
  - a submachine state references another machine and holds only entry/exit
    connection points [SEM-4]; a connector entry is a transition target and a
    connector exit a source, a standalone entry/exit in the machine reversed
    [SEM-5]
  - a transition ends on the border of a rectangular state, on the drawn circle
    of an initial/final, or on a rhombus vertex of a choice [EDGE-1..4]; the line
    ends in an arrow [EDGE-5]; a self-loop stays a loop [EDGE-8]
  - a set colour is drawn on the node or on the transition line and arrow
    [NODE-10, EDGE-14]
  - every entry/exit point has a name [SEM-7]; a submachine state references
    another machine of the document (or an external file), never its own, and
    its connector points are named after that machine's points [SEM-8]
  - a state has at most one `entry/` and one `exit/` block [STRUCT-10]; an
    event is not named entry, exit, do, propagate, block, defer or else
    (ANY and UNKNOWN are allowed) [TEXT-5]; `defer` is the whole behaviour of
    an internal reaction (`EVENT / defer`, nothing after it) and never labels
    a transition; `propagate`/`block` go with an event name [TEXT-6]; the
    machines of a document have distinct names [META-5]

Signal CHECK after a few edits; signal DONE when the whole diagram is drawn.

Ids are deterministic: the top-level elements of the machine G0 are n0, n1, ... in
creation order, the children of a state are parent::n0, parent::n1, ..., a transition
is source-target. Every edit answers with the new ids; use only ids you have seen,
and call inspect when unsure.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_p_confirm">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">PROMPT confirm</data>
      <data key="dData">A defect fired on your long history, given in the message above. Reproduce it from
the start document (one empty state machine G0) with as few commands as you can:
the shortest script that triggers the same failure. Every tool is available. When
your script is complete, signal REPRODUCED; the oracles then check it. If it does
not reproduce, you are told so and may try again. Call inspect to see the empty
document.

Ids are deterministic: the top-level elements of the machine G0 are n0, n1, ... in
creation order, the children of a state are parent::n0, parent::n1, ..., a transition
is source-target. Every edit answers with the new ids; use only ids you have seen,
and call inspect when unsure.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_init">
      <data key="dVertex">initial</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_editing">
      <data key="dName">Editing</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
tools.allow('create', 'connect', 'behave', 'arrange')
prompt.set('draw')

loop.FINISHED/
prompt.add('A text answer changes nothing: use a tool, or signal CHECK or DONE.')</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_applying">
      <data key="dName">Applying</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
tools.allow()</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_checking">
      <data key="dName">Checking</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
tools.allow()
oracle.check()</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_confirm">
      <data key="dName">Confirm</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
tools.allow_all()
prompt.set('confirm')

loop.FINISHED/
prompt.add('A text answer changes nothing: use a tool, or signal REPRODUCED.')</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_reproducing">
      <data key="dName">Reproducing</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
tools.allow()</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_confirming">
      <data key="dName">Confirming</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
tools.allow()
document.attempt()
oracle.check()</data>
    </node>
    <node id="d_done">
      <data key="dVertex">final</data>
    </node>
    <edge id="d_init-d_editing" source="d_init" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData"></data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_editing-d_applying" source="d_editing" target="d_applying">
      <data key="dData">document.STARTED/</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_applying-d_editing-1" source="d_applying" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">document.EDITED [document.edits &lt; 6]/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_applying-d_checking-1" source="d_applying" target="d_checking">
      <data key="dData">document.EDITED [document.edits &gt;= 6]/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_applying-d_editing-2" source="d_applying" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">document.REJECTED [document.rejections &lt; 5]/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_applying-d_done-1" source="d_applying" target="d_done">
      <data key="dData">document.REJECTED [document.rejections &gt;= 5]/
log.print('too many rejections')
tools.allow()
loop.stop()</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_applying-d_confirm-1" source="d_applying" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">document.CRASHED [event.new]/
document.branch(event.signature)
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_applying-d_editing-3" source="d_applying" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">document.CRASHED [not event.new]/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_editing-d_checking-1" source="d_editing" target="d_checking">
      <data key="dData">agent.CHECK [document.edits &gt; 0]/</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_checking-d_editing-1" source="d_checking" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">oracle.CLEAN/</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_checking-d_editing-2" source="d_checking" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">oracle.FOUND [event.new == 0]/</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_checking-d_confirm-1" source="d_checking" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">oracle.FOUND [event.new &gt; 0]/
document.branch(oracle.target)
prompt.add(oracle.last)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirm-d_reproducing" source="d_confirm" target="d_reproducing">
      <data key="dData">document.STARTED/</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_reproducing-d_confirm-1" source="d_reproducing" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">document.EDITED/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_reproducing-d_confirm-2" source="d_reproducing" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">document.REJECTED/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_reproducing-d_editing-1" source="d_reproducing" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">document.CRASHED [event.signature == document.target]/
register.confirm(document.target)
document.restore()
prompt.add('Reproduced and recorded. Back to the main line.')</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_reproducing-d_confirm-3" source="d_reproducing" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">document.CRASHED [event.signature != document.target]/
prompt.add(document.summary)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirm-d_confirming" source="d_confirm" target="d_confirming">
      <data key="dData">agent.REPRODUCED [document.edits &gt; 0]/</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirming-d_editing-1" source="d_confirming" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">oracle.FOUND [document.target in oracle.signatures]/
register.confirm(document.target)
document.restore()
prompt.add('Reproduced and recorded. Back to the main line.')</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirming-d_confirm-1" source="d_confirming" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">oracle.FOUND [document.target not in oracle.signatures and document.tries &lt; 3]/
prompt.add('Not reproduced: the defect did not fire. Try again from the start document.')</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirming-d_editing-2" source="d_confirming" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">oracle.FOUND [document.target not in oracle.signatures and document.tries &gt;= 3]/
document.restore()
prompt.add('Not reproduced; the long script is kept. Back to the main line.')</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirming-d_confirm-2" source="d_confirming" target="d_confirm">
      <data key="dData">oracle.CLEAN [document.tries &lt; 3]/
prompt.add('Not reproduced: the check was clean. Try again from the start document.')</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_confirming-d_editing-3" source="d_confirming" target="d_editing">
      <data key="dData">oracle.CLEAN [document.tries &gt;= 3]/
document.restore()
prompt.add('Not reproduced; the long script is kept. Back to the main line.')</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_editing-d_done-1" source="d_editing" target="d_done">
      <data key="dData">agent.DONE [document.edits == 0]/
tools.allow()
loop.stop()</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="d_editing-d_checking-2" source="d_editing" target="d_checking">
      <data key="dData">agent.DONE [document.edits &gt; 0]/</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
  <graph id="W" edgedefault="directed">
    <data key="dStateMachine"/>
    <data key="dName">Watchdog</data>
    <node id="w_c_loop">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT loop</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Loop</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_c_tools">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT tools</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Tools</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_c_log">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT log</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Log</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_c_budget">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT budget</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Budget

priority/ 10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_c_document">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT document</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Document</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_c_oracle">
      <data key="dNote">formal</data>
      <data key="dName">CGML_COMPONENT oracle</data>
      <data key="dData">type/ Oracle

profile/ stress</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_init">
      <data key="dVertex">initial</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_watching">
      <data key="dName">Watching</data>
      <data key="dData">entry/
budget.limit(requests=document.max_calls, seconds=document.max_seconds)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="w_done">
      <data key="dVertex">final</data>
    </node>
    <edge id="w_init-w_watching" source="w_init" target="w_watching">
      <data key="dData"></data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="w_watching-w_done" source="w_watching" target="w_done">
      <data key="dData">budget.EXCEEDED/
log.print('stopped:', event.kind)
document.stop()
oracle.stop()
tools.allow()
loop.stop()</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
